I return home from the market.
I go to the kitchen to make lunch.
I place the vegetables and chicken on the table.
I open the recipe on my phone.
I read it out loud.
"First, wash the chicken thoroughly," I read.
I take that half a kilo of chicken and wash it in water.
I set it aside in a bowl.
I look at the next line in the recipe.
"Then, finely chop the onions and tomatoes."
I take two large onions.
I chop them into small pieces.
After that, I chop three tomatoes the same way.
"After that, crush the ginger and green chilies," I read again.
I do that too.
I also set aside two spoons of masala powder.
Now everything to make the curry is ready.
Now I can start cooking.
